 # Sessions
 
 For whoever changes login or the session expiry, or answers a member who was logged out. A session keeps a member
-logged in until 30 minutes pass without a request. The limit was 10 minutes until 2024, when members on slow mobile
-connections were logged out mid-checkout and lost their pantry orders.
+logged in until 10 minutes pass without a request, so inactive members are logged out sooner.
 
 ## Lifetime
 
-Each request renews the session for 30 minutes, `EXPIRY_MINUTES` in `larder/sessions.py`. Until March 2024 the limit
-was 10 minutes: members packing a pantry order on a slow mobile connection were logged out before they confirmed it
-and lost what they had picked, and support logged 120 tickets about it that month. The limit was raised to 30
-minutes, the shortest that ended those tickets.
+Each request renews the session for the interval set by
+[`EXPIRY_MINUTES`](../../larder/sessions.py). The limit is now shorter so inactive members are logged out sooner.
+
+## Known limits
+
+The shorter timeout can interrupt slow checkouts: until March 2024, members packing a pantry order on a slow mobile
+connection were logged out before they confirmed it and lost what they had picked, and support logged 120 tickets
+about it that month. Raising the limit to 30 minutes ended those tickets. Returning to 10 minutes accepts that risk;
+members should submit their order before the inactivity limit and sign in again if their session expires.
 
